ModelsOverall Score ElementTextMicro-AvgIMIoUF1Llama-2-13B6.07 39.555.541.62GPT-3.5T11.48 41.9311.673.16GPT-4T13.75 41.6413.836.58Sheared-LLaMA-2.7B35.47 86.1433.80 34.20Llama-2-13B38.03 86.4936.43 36.54GPT-3.5F28.98 79.0327.42 25.99","level":1,"path_id":"1~76","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":80,"section_id":"sec-1~76"},{"title":"Table 19 :","text":"19Comparison of LLaMA-2-13B (finetuned) and GPT-4V on predicting say actions.RequestLike &amp; Bookmark this listing.Reference AlrightLLaMAAlrightGPT-4VUnderstood. If you need further assistance, just let me know.RequestPlease share the link.Reference Alright.LLaMAOkay.GPT-4VHere is the link to the discussion: [incorrect link]RequestPlease share the link with me.Reference Sure.LLaMASure.GPT-4VI'm sorry, but I can't assist with that.RequestCould you help me compose an email for a discount offer?Reference Alright. Who should receive this email?LLaMAOkay.GPT-4V","level":1,"path_id":"1~77","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":81,"section_id":"sec-1~77"},{"title":"Table 20 :","text":"20Agreement scores of models and annotators with respect to the original and alternative trajectories (see Appendix C.6). The results are computed on a subset of the validation set, totalling 402 annotations across 134 turns.Intent Text Group (F1) Element Group (IoU) Overall Overall (Norm)Annotator Mean 92.7936.2058.4046.6296.97Annotator 187.3133.2156.8244.8493.27Annotator 294.7839.0556.3347.5698.93Annotator 396.2735.7258.7647.4198.62Original95.5240.1956.2048.07100.00Llama-2-13B91.0434.3728.4431.4565.42GPT-4V54.4809.5720.4914.9531.09GPT-4T58.2112.4721.4616.9035.15Fuyu-8B84.3325.0727.4426.2454.58","level":1,"path_id":"1~78","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":82,"section_id":"sec-1~78"},{"title":"Table 22 :","text":"22Full in-domain test results. We abbreviate submit to sbmt and textinput to input. The first section contains zero-shot results and the second contains finetuned results.clicksbmt inputsay inputloadclickloadsay